<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ezzelino III da Romano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1194–1259</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ezzelino III da Romano was a Ghibelline lord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/march-of-treviso">March of Treviso</a> and an ally of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>. From the 1220s to the 1250s he dominated Verona, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, ruling with a cruelty that made him a byword for tyranny. A papal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> was proclaimed against him, and he was wounded and captured at Cassano in 1259, dying soon after.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ezzelino-iii-da-romano.jpg" alt="Ezzelino III da Romano" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cristofano dell'Altissimo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Ezzelino_III_da_Romano_(by_Cristofano_dell%27Altissimo).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
